WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.543
Imagine a shop worker is caught taking money from the till. The manager ends their job. This is called dismissal.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:24.017
Dismissal means the employer ends a worker's job because of something the worker has done, or cannot do. Redundancy is different: the job itself is no longer needed, so it is not the worker's fault.

00:00:25.150 --> 00:00:36.182
Fair reasons include serious misconduct, such as theft, violence or breaking safety rules, repeated lateness or absence, and being unable to do the job properly.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:55.551
Businesses usually follow a disciplinary procedure first, for example a verbal warning, then a written warning. Dismissal comes only if the problem continues. For serious misconduct, such as theft, a worker may be dismissed without earlier warnings, but only after a fair investigation.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:01:03.893
Unfair dismissal is ending someone's job for a reason the law does not allow, such as their age, religion, gender or race.

00:01:04.450 --> 00:01:11.713
To answer an Outline question, give one fair reason, set it in the business's own work, then add the consequence for the business.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:29.700
Here is a real question from Paper one in November twenty twenty-four. Outline one reason why Saha may dismiss an employee. It is worth two marks. Saha makes robots for hospitals, hotels and restaurants.

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:38.762
Mark one is the reason. Serious misconduct, such as stealing robot parts or ignoring safety rules when assembling robots.

00:01:39.350 --> 00:01:51.965
Mark two is the development. This could damage robots or injure other workers, so orders to hospitals and restaurants are delayed and Saha's reputation suffers.

00:01:53.100 --> 00:02:01.945
Mistake one: giving a redundancy reason. Needing fewer staff is not the worker's fault, so it is not dismissal.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:08.009
Mistake two: giving an unfair reason, such as age or religion. That would break the law.

00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:24.669
Now you try. A bus company has a driver who keeps arriving late for shifts, even after warnings. Outline one reason the company may dismiss this driver. Pause and decide.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:40.117
The reason is repeated lateness. When the driver is late, buses leave late and passengers miss their connections. The company gets complaints and may lose customers.

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:49.278
That is the pattern for this type: give a fair reason, set it in the business, then add the consequence. Now try the practice questions.
